ered and their I/O tied together, the PWM, TACH and POT pins would be driven by two devices at once. This could cause contention, wrong fan speed control, unreliable tach sensing, or damage to the I/O pins.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.45\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The netlist places two different microcontrollers, U2 (ATtiny45) and U3 (ATtiny13), on identical signal, power and ground nets, which would double-drive PWM, TACH and POT if both are populated. Power, pull-up, transistor and regulator connections otherwise match standard practice and the stated values, so the main concern is this duplicated MCU.\"\n}",
